{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Behold</b> — R. Moses haKohen says: behold, in the Torah it is written that the descent of the manna was at first in many stations, before the smiting of the rock at Rephidim. And furthermore: the anger of HaShem did not burn on account of the manna, for it says, <i>ואש נשקה ביעקב</i> (\"and fire was kindled in Jacob\"), and after it is written, <i>וימטר עליהן מן לאכול</i> (\"and He rained upon them manna to eat\"). And behold, Scripture jumbled its words, placing the later before the earlier and reversing this, and he did not worry about this, for it is explicitly clear among us in the Torah of Moses." "<b>Can He give bread also</b> — concerning the manna. The meaning: can He give it continually without interruption, and like it is <i>הורד עדיך</i> [in my opinion]. Said Abraham ibn Ezra the author: these words contain error, and I shall explain everything." "<b>He has prepared a table</b> — concerning meat; the craving was for the graves of lust, and this is to set the table. And the word <i>לחם</i> [bread] means flesh, as in <i>את קרבני לחמי לחם אשה</i> [the food of my offering, the food of the offering made by fire], and the witness [is] <i>אם יכין שאר לעמו</i> [if he prepares food for his people], for the meaning is doubled, for <i>שאר</i> means flesh."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {0 "The referent of 'he did not worry' is ambiguous; likely R. Moses haKohen, who dismisses the apparent chronological disorder because the correct sequence is explicit in the Torah.", 1 "The phrase הורד עדיך [bring down to you] — its source and application are unclear; rendered hyper-literally.", 2 "Ibn Ezra's lemma here differs from the MT verse text of Ps 78:20; he appears to be addressing the phrase לחם יוכל תת and treating לחם as 'flesh' based on multiple wordplay witnesses."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:08.643763452Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}